### Health Check Endpoint — JetBrains HTTP Client
### Usage: Open in WebStorm/IntelliJ and click ▶ against a running local server (npm run dev)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3010/api

### GET /health — Liveness check (no auth required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###
# Expected 200 Response Shape:
#
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK
# Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
#
# {
#   "status": "ok",
#   "timestamp": "2026-02-23T12:00:00.000Z",
#   "uptimeSeconds": 42,
#   "version": "1.0.0"
# }
#
# Field descriptions:
#   status        — always "ok" when the service is healthy
#   timestamp     — ISO 8601 UTC datetime of when this request was processed
#   uptimeSeconds — integer seconds since the Node process started (>= 0)
#   version       — matches the "version" field in package.json

### Health Check
# Confirms the backend is running and returns basic runtime info
GET http://localhost:3010/api/health

### Expected response shape (example)
# {
#   "status": "ok",
#   "timestamp": "2026-02-24T04:55:15.063Z",
#   "uptimeSeconds": 53,
#   "version": "1.0.0"
# }
